  "explanation": "The process is experiencing a shift in the composition of the combined A/C feed stream. The high contribution of XMEAS(25) (C in reactor feed) showing an increase alongside XMEAS(23) (A in reactor feed) showing a decrease indicates a change in the A/C ratio. Although the total A feed flow (XMEAS(1)) is elevated, the concentration of A in the mixed feed has dropped, while the concentration of C has risen. This pattern is consistent with a step change in the A/C feed ratio from stream 4 (IDV(1)) or random variations in the composition of the A, B, and C feed (IDV(8)). The elevated total flow of A (XMEAS(1)) without a corresponding proportional increase in its concentration in the reactor feed suggests that the C component from stream 4 is dominating the mixture change, potentially due to a reduced availability or pressure loss affecting the A component more significantly, or simply a compositional shift in the feed header."
